A||||4||Adrift||Anyone installed $40 ebay "Xenon" upgrade?||||1||
Z||000000||Adrift||11-19-2001||08:42 PM||||I just bought a set and can't get them working... has anyone been able to?<P>I've been told here that the headlights are controlled by a circuit breaker - do the xenon bulbs draws more amps, tripping the breaker?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Jay||11-19-2001||09:22 PM||||I just went to Canadian tire and bought the Bosch hologen upgrade kit.  It came with the lens and 2 hologen lights which you can change to any color you like.  I think it cost me about $60 Canadian.<P>------------------<BR>Jay<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig2_copy_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fiero_Freak||11-19-2001||10:00 PM||||I put mine in no problem.  They worked just like the stock ones only a little brighter. I think they draw less current than my old lights... I think they were really old.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero_Left_01.jpg">  <BR>Two '87 GT's...<BR>   ...Double Trouble||||reg||1
Z||000003||IwannaIRM||11-19-2001||10:49 PM||||Have had mine in for over a month.  No voltage or battery drain problems observed.<P>And they are <B>much</B> brighter than the stock ones.  You will enjoy.<P>I paid $50 for mine including new headlight motors.<P><P>------------------<BR>AIM - SWags2933<P>84 Fiero SE (being modified)<BR>88 Formula||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroJoe||11-20-2001||02:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Adrift:<BR><B>I just bought a set and can't get them working... has anyone been able to?<P>I've been told here that the headlights are controlled by a circuit breaker - do the xenon bulbs draws more amps, tripping the breaker?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>If you're talking about about the set from <A HREF="http://www.prostreetlighting.com" TARGET=_blank>www.prostreetlighting.com</A>  that is on ebay, I have installed those with only one problem:  The seal of the two peices of glass of the main housing (same size as 6054 bulb) is thinner than a regular 6054, so the housing would rattle a little bit in the housing.  What I did was silicone the glass housings to the metal trim/retainer ring.<P>Other than that, I had to send the bulbs (not the housings) back because the low filament in one of them busted after about 500 miles.  They gave me a new set, no problem.  The new bulbs have worked perfectly for a long time.||||reg||1
